  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Star∴eternal is a Nightshelf fire-technology that channels captured volcanic cores through bone-lattice conduits, granting practitioners perception and manipulation of pressure-depth magic across vast distances. It originated in Thrall☽ Vavmastius, an advanced fire-research site, reportedly from the Communion's study of Rumzunkaidkak — a claim I can neither confirm nor dismiss, as the relevant ice-strata in the Foundation Depths are thermally scarred beyond legibility.
    
    ## Procedure and Function
    
    The process is both ritual and surgical. Fire-cores are sutured directly into the practitioner's marrow; bone becomes translucent, threaded with ash-light. The result is a sensory capacity that defies conventional taxonomy — perception of pressure-tremors through solid ice, resonance with distant water currents, awareness of depth itself as a navigable dimension. Operators have demonstrated perception through ice exceeding 400 body-lengths, though I note the measurement methodology is unspecified. Sustaining the connection requires a steady feed of one Class II fire-core per half-shift.
    
    ## Limitations
    
    The fundamental material constraint of Star∴eternal is thermal expansion: fire-core heat expands bone-lattice faster than the grain structure can absorb, and conduits fracture under sustained load. Corrupted ice-stone substrate lined with bioluminescent fungi has been demonstrated to function as a thermal valve — the fungi metabolize excess heat, keeping the lattice below fracture stress — though the technique requires access to corruption sites.
    
    ## Cost
    
    The technology consumes its carriers. ☽'Retenusus the Undimmed, a Nightshelf practitioner, burned from the inside out. Lovumruius~ Domina, another practitioner of note, survives but suffers involuntary flipper contractions the Communion terms *fire-memory*. The pattern across known practitioners — diminished speech, increasing preference for darkness — is consistent enough to constitute a degenerative profile rather than anecdote.
    
    ## Strategic Significance
    
    Star∴eternal's practitioner base is broad: the Collective☽ Of Led∴merch, the Midnight Claws, the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, and individual operatives including Shadow-Broker Nyla all employ it for surveillance and deep-tunnel navigation. Its utility is constrained by the same fire-core supply crisis now destabilizing the wider Nightshelf economy. A technology that demands constant feeding becomes a liability when the feed runs short.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771582178671_0", anchor: "a Nightshelf fire-technology that channels captured volcanic cores", text: "In my annotation on the Shelf Crushing Offense I called Star∴eternal 'an Aurora Stack harvesting technique.' Here I introduce it as Nightshelf fire-technology. Both are true, which is the entertaining part. The bone-lattice conduit work is pure Nightshelf — no Aurora adept would suture a fire-core into marrow. But the resonance principles governing the perception at distance? Aurora crystal-divination methodology, stripped of its theological dress and wired into a volcanic power source. The Nightshelf did not invent this. They *converted* it. And the Aurora histories do not mention the original because admitting it existed would mean admitting it was stolen, which would mean admitting it was worth stealing.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582178671_1", anchor: "perception through ice exceeding 400 body-lengths", text: "Four hundred. Not 'approximately four hundred,' not 'between three and five hundred.' Four hundred. My policy on round numbers in unverified claims is well established.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582178671_2", anchor: "the Midnight Claws, the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, and individual operatives including Shadow-Broker Nyla", text: "A formally dissolved syndicate, a broker who confessed to murder before a foreign council, and a merchant guild hemorrhaging territory. Star∴eternal's practitioner roster reads less like a strategic asset and more like a list of penguins the Nightshelf would prefer you forgot about. One wonders whether the degenerative profile described above is a medical side effect or a security feature.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
